; 1.80 m overall, the length a real composite lead shipped at, split so the
; breakouts are part of it: a 1.50 m trunk (50 x 30 mm) plus a 150 mm tail at each
; end (5 x 30 mm). Buying length with segment COUNT rather than a longer segment
; keeps the boot and the minimum bend radius where cable.tscn tuned them in
; millimetres. 80 particles against that lead's 60, so reckon on ~1.4 ms per
; physics tick — it is a spawned object, not one per station.
;
; 2.2 mm cords, thinner than the N64 lead's 3 mm: Sega's lead is a slim one, and the
; plug's moulding hugs its shield, so the ribbon has to fit a 6.8 mm boot. Three of
; them make a 6.6 mm ribbon. The cords are drawn from
; ribbon_colors and the trunk needs no rope_color of its own.
;
; collision_radius is the ribbon's HALF-WIDTH, not the standoff over the tube that
; cable.tscn uses. The solver only ever collides the centreline, so on a round cord
; the radius is the cord; on a ribbon it has to cover the outermost cord or that one
; sinks through whatever the cable is lying on. 2.2 mm pitch x 2 gaps / 2 + 1.1 mm tube
; = 3.3 mm. Get this wrong low and the outer cord dips under the floor whenever the
; ribbon happens to lie on edge.
;
; The plug's strain relief is sized against this — see CORD_R in Tools/gen/gen_genesis_av.gd,
; which has to end wider than the ribbon it grips. Change one and change the other.
;
; The cost is that a ribbon lying FLAT now floats 2.2 mm rather than resting on
; its tube. Both cannot be right from one radius on one centreline; poke-through
; reads worse than clearance. Fixing it properly means giving the solver the
; ribbon frame so the standoff can follow |side . normal|, which is a
; VerletRope change, not a scene value.
[node name="VerletRope" type="VerletRope" parent="."]
segment_count = 50
segment_length = 0.03
constraint_iterations = 8
bend_stiffness = 0.2
tube_radius = 0.0011
tube_sides = 6
smoothing = 2
surface_collision_mask = 7
collision_radius = 0.0033
self_collision = true
end_align_stiffness = 0.7
end_stiffness = 0.45
end_stiff_segments = 2
fray_segments_start = 5
fray_segments_end = 5
fray_taper_segments = 3
